|introduction      = 

|release history   = The retail release was published by Sierra Entertainment up until the publisher lost all publishing rights to Valve's titles in 2005. Valve subsequently partnered with Electronic Arts to distribute later retail versions of the game and future titles. The macOS (OS X) version was released in 2010 and the Linux version later in 2013, both coinciding with the launch of Steam on their respective platforms.

|current state     = Like most of Valve's library, the game still receives bug fixes and general maintenance updates. It also enjoys a large community base, and various mods are released regularly.

With the 20th Anniversary Update for the base Half-Life 2 on November 15, 2024, both Episodes and [[Half-Life 2: Lost Coast|Lost Coast]] were merged into the default game (as the {{code|hl2_complete}} "mod", individual parts accessible from the main menu) and were moved to the Tools section in the Steam library. Purchasing them as a single package became the only way of obtaining them, with prior owners of any part of the collection receiving any missing content. Only the base game's store page is accessible from search.<ref>{{Refurl|url=https://www.half-life.com/en/halflife2/20th|title=Half-Life 2 Anniversary Update|date=2025-09-10}}</ref><ref>{{Refurl|url=https://store.steampowered.com/news/app/220/view/6633333780228604001|title=Half-Life 2 - Half-Life 2 20th Anniversary Update - Steam News|date=2025-09-10}}</ref>
