{{Introduction
|introduction      = '''''Cyberpunk 2077''''' is a {{Glossary:singleplayer}} {{Glossary:open world}} {{Glossary:action}} game developed by [[Company:CD Projekt Red|CD Projekt Red]] and published by [[Company:CD Projekt|CD Projekt]]. It is based on Mike Pondsmith's ''Cyberpunk'' tabletop game series.

|release history   = Initially announced in May 2012 and featured at E3 2019, the game was set to be released on April 16, 2020, followed by a delay to September 17, which was further delayed to November 19, and subsequently the final date of December 10.<ref name="date" /><ref>{{Refurl|url=https://www.eurogamer.net/articles/2015-08-17-inside-the-witcher-3-launch|title=I was there when The Witcher 3 launched |date=2020-06-20}}</ref><ref>{{Refurl|url=https://twitter.com/CyberpunkGame/status/1273647385294626816|title=Twitter - @CyberpunkGame - June 19, 2019|date=2020-06-20}}</ref> Upon launch, the game had around 830k concurrent players on Steam, a new record for a single-player game on the platform,<ref>{{Refurl|url=https://www.pcgamer.com/cyberpunk-2077-has-over-a-million-concurrent-players-on-steam/|title=PC Gamer: Cyberpunk 2077 has over a million concurrent players on Steam|date=2020-12-10}}</ref> but was also affected by a number of bugs and issues ranging from minor visual issues, performance issues and crashes, as well as game-breaking bugs that necessitated resetting to an older save, if one were available.<ref>{{Refurl|url=https://www.windowscentral.com/cyberpunk-2077-known-bugs-and-launch-issues|title=Windows Central - List of Cyberpunk 2077 known bugs and launch issues|date=2022-09-17}}</ref> During the first weeks after launch three hotfixes were released to address some of the most critical issues.

On January 13, 2021 [[Company:CD Projekt Red|CD Projekt Red]] released a statement of [https://steamcommunity.com/games/1091500/announcements/detail/3056222849545625199 their commitment to quality] and laid out a roadmap for further updates and improvements to be released during 2021, which they largely kept to, although some of the later planned updates were pushed to 2022.<ref>{{Refurl|url=https://www.pcgamer.com/cyberpunk-2077-fixes-and-free-dlc-have-all-been-delayed-until-2022/|title=PC Gamer - Cyberpunk 2077 fixes and free DLC have all been delayed until 2022|date=2022-09-17}}</ref> 

The game's major expansion, titled ''Phantom Liberty''<ref name="Phantom Liberty">[https://www.cyberpunk.net/en/news/45460/announcing-cyberpunk-2077-phantom-liberty ''Announcing Cyberpunk 2077: Phantom Liberty'' – Cyberpunk.net.]</ref><ref>{{Refurl|url=https://twitter.com/CyberpunkGame/status/1641482504526876672|title=Cyberpunk 2077 "Exciting news, chooms... - Cyberpunk 2077 - Twitter|date=2023-03-30}}</ref>, was released on September 26, 2023.

On July 16, 2025 the game was launched on Mac with Apple Silicon.<ref name="update2-3"></ref>

